0..78 Comment "// Grade orders that do not settle as `true`, each refused `EndpointMismatch`."
79..81 Comment "//"
82..158 Comment "// An order that does not hold is refused by the conversion that settles one"
159..235 Comment "// that does. An algebra over the native integers decides nothing, since the"
236..290 Comment "// kernel reads a closed native as an opaque constant."
291..293 Comment "//"
294..368 Comment "// The checker evaluates `Usage.le` and `Count.le` over closed constructor"
369..442 Comment "// data and reaches `false`. `Bytes.le(2, 4)` stays the integer primitive"
443..491 Comment "// applied, which no conversion takes to `true`."
492..494 Comment "//"
495..571 Comment "// - see: `../../model/effects/grade-algebra.gandr` — the orders that hold"
572..653 Comment "// - see: `../../../library/std/src/grade.gandr` — `Grade`, `Usage` and `Count`"
654..722 Comment "// - see: #2378 — a closed native reads back as an opaque constant"
723..781 Comment "// - see: #3287 — grade algebras as models of one theory"
783..822 Comment "// `Grade`, `Use`, `Usage` and `Count`."
